# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Git LFS is explicitly NOT used in this repository, by design.
#
# The point of this project is a zero-dependency, zero-cost static JSON API:
# data lives as plain, human-readable, diffable text in git and is served
# directly from GitHub Pages / raw.githubusercontent.com.
#
# If `git lfs` ever rewrites these paths, the deployed site would serve LFS
# pointer files instead of data, and every consumer would break silently.
#
# `-filter` disables any clean/smudge filter (which is how LFS hooks itself in)
# while keeping the files plain text so `git diff` stays readable — that
# readability is what makes git-as-DB workable.
#
# Attributes later in this file win, so `git lfs track` appending its own
# filter=lfs line would override these. scripts/check-no-lfs.mjs is the actual
# enforcement and runs in CI on every push.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.json -filter text eol=lf
data/** -filter text eol=lf
*.png -filter
*.svg -filter text eol=lf
